                <pb facs="0619" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg493"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.6363/157: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Albania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grant-Smith</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-02-04T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 4,
                                1925—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. The Standard Oil Company of New York informs the Department that it has
                    received word of renewed activity on the part of Anglo-Persian in Albania. The
                    company is disposed to send a representative to Albania should the situation
                    warrant. Please make a brief telegraphic report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
